WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.000 --> 00:01.510
[Disclaimer: All events depicted in this series are fictional]

3
00:01.530 --> 00:02.340
[and created for entertainment purposes only.]

4
00:02.360 --> 00:03.250
[Viewer discretion is advised.]

5
00:20.990 --> 00:22.020
Khwankhao

6
00:22.050 --> 00:23.820
took her friends from Bangkok trekking in the forest,

7
00:23.850 --> 00:25.260
but it's been three days now.

8
00:25.290 --> 00:26.330
Still no sign of them.

9
00:26.350 --> 00:27.600
I'll be back as soon as I can.

10
00:27.620 --> 00:29.820
I thought Paran was gonna turn down work

11
00:29.840 --> 00:32.090
after the monk warned him about the misfortune coming his way.

12
00:32.110 --> 00:33.420
This misfortune hanging over you

13
00:33.450 --> 00:35.090
is grave enough to cost you your life.

14
00:35.120 --> 00:36.350
What should we do, Khem?

15
00:36.370 --> 00:37.510
Should we help Master instead?

16
00:37.540 --> 00:38.470
We should go to the set.

17
00:38.500 --> 00:40.260
They're waiting for our help, too.

18
00:40.290 --> 00:43.540
Those kids are being hunted by malicious spirits

19
00:43.570 --> 00:46.280
that are thralls of a sorcerer.

20
00:46.300 --> 00:47.960
Please grant me the chance

21
00:47.990 --> 00:50.990
to return to my beloved.

22
00:54.530 --> 01:17.650
[Incanting]

23
01:21.810 --> 01:22.990
Those brats...

24
01:23.010 --> 01:24.110
Where the hell did they go?

25
01:49.070 --> 01:50.210
You alright, Max?

26
01:51.660 --> 01:52.720
I'm good.

27
01:53.310 --> 01:54.410
What about you, Pleng?

28
01:54.670 --> 01:55.479
Are you okay?

29
01:56.220 --> 01:58.210
I'm fine. I'm not as badly hurt as you are.

30
02:02.190 --> 02:04.200
Khao, hanging in there?

31
02:26.380 --> 02:27.980
The Seven-Layer Crystal Wall spell

32
02:28.010 --> 02:30.050
is still masking our presence from those spirits.

33
02:30.329 --> 02:31.710
Let's catch our breath while we can.

34
02:47.340 --> 02:53.350
♪ A blessed day has come, with fortune aglow ♪

35
02:53.380 --> 02:59.430
♪ Graceful offerings are arranged in a row ♪

36
02:59.450 --> 03:03.680
♪ Sacred threads and rings of gold, ♪

37
03:03.700 --> 03:06.580
♪ Jewels and necklaces, precious to behold ♪

38
03:06.600 --> 03:08.820
♪ A feast overflowing with plenty to spare ♪

39
03:08.850 --> 03:11.660
♪ All things prepared with the greatest care ♪

40
03:11.690 --> 03:14.230
♪ Betel rolls and areca nuts are laid there ♪

41
03:14.250 --> 03:17.230
♪ Everything adorned and displayed with flair ♪

42
03:17.250 --> 03:23.300
♪ "May your vital forces come forth" ♪

43
03:23.320 --> 03:27.430
♪ May your vital forces come forth ♪

44
03:28.070 --> 03:31.710
♪ O vital forces, beyond the skies, ♪

45
03:31.740 --> 03:33.950
♪ In distant realms where your souls fly, ♪

46
03:33.970 --> 03:35.770
♪ Heed the call and now arise, ♪

47
03:35.790 --> 03:42.600
♪ Return to where your vessels lie ♪

48
04:30.520 --> 04:31.290
Here you go.

49
04:32.159 --> 04:33.020
Thanks.

50
04:37.650 --> 04:38.540
Here.

51
04:40.909 --> 04:41.750
Thanks.

52
04:42.450 --> 04:44.420
- Spitting image. - Spitting image.

53
04:58.650 --> 05:00.520
You drink the exact same thing as me.

54
05:01.860 --> 05:02.920
Bold and aromatic.

55
05:03.200 --> 05:05.490
It tastes like freshly brewed coffee.

56
05:05.780 --> 05:07.510
I could stay up busting ghosts all night with this.

57
05:12.780 --> 05:15.500
Could I ask for your advice on something?

58
05:16.800 --> 05:17.690
Sure.

59
05:18.160 --> 05:19.450
I was wondering,

60
05:19.470 --> 05:23.370
since you've been seeing ghosts your whole life,

61
05:23.450 --> 05:25.910
you wouldn't be scared of them anymore, right?

62
05:26.180 --> 05:28.480
You'd only fear spirits that mean harm.

63
05:29.930 --> 05:30.670
Exactly.

64
05:30.890 --> 05:33.650
You really did your homework.

65
05:39.820 --> 05:41.680
Frost, didn't you have a question for Jet?

66
05:43.470 --> 05:44.380
Go ahead.

67
05:44.400 --> 05:45.120
Oh...

68
05:45.980 --> 05:46.690
Right.

69
05:47.659 --> 05:49.590
Well, the catering lady just taught me this,

70
05:49.960 --> 05:52.810
so I'd like you to check if my accent is alright.

71
05:54.200 --> 05:56.290
"I miss Master so much."

72
05:58.240 --> 05:59.210
Whoa.

73
05:59.950 --> 06:01.520
Why are you so adorable?

74
06:02.300 --> 06:03.470
Stop it, Tol.

75
06:06.860 --> 06:09.530
- You're exactly like us... - You're exactly like us...

76
06:10.570 --> 06:12.910
Hello, Khem.

77
06:12.940 --> 06:15.470
Sorry, I was dealing with the art department.

78
06:16.030 --> 06:17.240
Sorry to keep you waiting.

79
06:20.740 --> 06:21.450
Coach Dol,

80
06:22.040 --> 06:24.450
that's Namprung over there.

81
06:28.580 --> 06:30.760
- Hi, Coach Dol. - Hello, Khem.

82
06:30.790 --> 06:32.050
Hi, guys.

83
06:33.590 --> 06:34.600
Identical.

84
06:36.170 --> 06:36.760
Wait.

85
06:38.060 --> 06:40.340
King, Namprung, Tol, Frost.

86
06:40.360 --> 06:42.750
Why aren't you in costume yet, babes?

87
06:42.780 --> 06:44.020
Get changed so we can roll

88
06:44.050 --> 06:45.330
while we still have time.

89
06:45.360 --> 06:47.390
If we cancel another shoot, I'm gonna lose it.

90
06:47.659 --> 06:48.760
Move now.

91
06:50.180 --> 06:51.050
Go on.

92
06:52.730 --> 06:55.700
Let's go over our lines while getting our hair and makeup done, King.

93
06:56.720 --> 06:57.980
I've already memorized mine.

94
06:58.620 --> 06:59.920
I feel bad for the crew.

95
06:59.940 --> 07:01.840
We've called off this scene multiple times,

96
07:02.260 --> 07:03.560
so I want to wrap it up fast.

97
07:10.830 --> 07:13.980
Poor guys. It's their debut series, and nothing is going smoothly.

98
07:14.660 --> 07:18.190
I hope this series blows up for them.

99
07:19.740 --> 07:20.810
Anyway,

100
07:20.970 --> 07:22.750
thanks for coming to help.

101
07:22.810 --> 07:24.210
We're happy to help.

102
07:24.410 --> 07:26.670
Could you walk us through

103
07:26.690 --> 07:27.970
everything that happened?

104
07:40.140 --> 07:43.290
The location department usually preps the site in advance.

105
07:43.909 --> 07:46.240
That day, everyone happened to show up late.

106
07:59.100 --> 08:00.380
Where are you guys?

107
08:02.150 --> 08:04.150
Hey, you're supposed to be here first.

108
08:04.430 --> 08:05.020
Oh...

109
08:57.880 --> 09:01.110
After that, everyone went to a temple to make merit.

110
09:01.510 --> 09:02.860
We thought that'd be the end of it.

111
09:03.930 --> 09:05.250
Turns out,

112
09:06.920 --> 09:07.980
it only got worse.

113
09:08.170 --> 09:09.310
Cut.

114
09:10.710 --> 09:13.650
Hey, you're the ghost here.

115
09:13.670 --> 09:15.680
You're supposed to scare Khem,

116
09:15.700 --> 09:19.160
not jump at every rustling bush.

117
09:19.190 --> 09:22.060
Coach Dol, I think I saw something on the left side of Camera A's frame.

118
09:22.310 --> 09:23.360
Kin, play it back.

119
09:23.440 --> 09:24.900
- On it. - Right at the end.

120
09:24.920 --> 09:25.810
What is it?

121
09:26.110 --> 09:26.930
The very end.

122
09:27.500 --> 09:28.520
What now?

123
09:29.040 --> 09:29.890
Keep rewinding.

124
09:33.210 --> 09:34.410
- Left where? You mean... Whoa. - There.

125
09:34.430 --> 09:35.480
Right there.

126
09:35.510 --> 09:36.670
Wait, hold on.

127
09:38.780 --> 09:40.000
Shit.

128
09:45.850 --> 09:47.210
[It's always me]

129
09:47.230 --> 09:48.080
That's what happened.

130
09:48.840 --> 09:50.350
When we played it back again,

131
09:50.640 --> 09:51.540
it was gone.

132
09:56.110 --> 09:58.020
Pardon me for speaking up,

133
09:58.850 --> 09:59.700
but...

134
10:00.060 --> 10:01.570
I've had this strange feeling

135
10:01.780 --> 10:04.140
ever since we got here.

136
10:04.610 --> 10:06.800
Have you considered changing locations?

137
10:06.870 --> 10:09.040
We'd miss our air date.

138
10:09.260 --> 10:12.930
We were planning to ask the monks at the nearby temple for help.

139
10:12.960 --> 10:14.890
You know, the one we visited to make merit.

140
10:15.210 --> 10:16.720
But once we went there again,

141
10:18.010 --> 10:19.490
it was completely abandoned.

142
10:25.360 --> 10:26.690
Jet, can you handle this?

143
10:30.130 --> 10:30.800
Yeah.

144
11:12.520 --> 11:13.420
Coach Dol,

145
11:14.210 --> 11:15.640
we had an agreement.

146
11:16.090 --> 11:18.140
All the cast and crew

147
11:18.160 --> 11:19.900
were supposed to wait at the base camp.

148
11:21.500 --> 11:26.580
Come on, I asked you all to come here.

149
11:26.610 --> 11:29.430
How could I leave you on your own?

150
11:29.450 --> 11:30.730
Besides,

151
11:30.870 --> 11:33.440
the cast is already here,

152
11:33.470 --> 11:35.380
so they might as well watch the ritual.

153
11:35.400 --> 11:38.260
It'll help them get into character for the scenes.

154
11:38.640 --> 11:39.210
Right?

155
11:39.230 --> 11:42.520
I promise we'll stay quiet and out of the way.

156
11:46.790 --> 11:49.200
Jet, it's the auspicious hour.

157
11:51.310 --> 11:52.820
Gather in close.

158
11:54.610 --> 11:56.390
Focus your minds, everyone.

159
12:05.930 --> 12:39.100
[Incanting]

160
13:08.300 --> 13:10.620
Will you not leave us be?

161
13:18.910 --> 13:19.670
Elder,

162
13:21.190 --> 13:24.060
we only seek your permission to film a series here.

163
13:25.540 --> 13:27.990
We will dedicate merit to you in return.

164
14:07.140 --> 14:08.080
He's gone.

165
14:09.390 --> 14:10.960
The other spirits are also gone.

166
14:11.830 --> 14:13.430
But isn't it strange?

167
14:13.840 --> 14:15.200
Why was it so easy?

168
14:20.060 --> 14:21.270
Isn't easy a good thing?

169
14:21.810 --> 14:23.710
It means my craft is still sharp.

170
14:27.300 --> 14:29.100
I really asked the right person.

171
14:29.120 --> 14:31.000
Thank you so much.

172
14:34.680 --> 14:35.340
Let's go.

173
14:35.580 --> 14:36.460
Pack it up.

174
14:37.060 --> 14:37.690
Alright.

175
14:37.790 --> 14:38.360
Brilliant.

176
14:38.600 --> 14:40.500
Come on, guys. Get ready.

177
14:40.950 --> 14:44.510
Lighting and art department, head onto the set.

178
14:44.540 --> 14:46.650
Let's wrap early today, babes.

179
14:47.010 --> 14:48.090
Come on.

180
14:48.590 --> 14:51.100
We're going home early, babes.

181
15:06.450 --> 15:07.330
Hold on.

182
15:08.160 --> 15:09.550
Has anyone seen Coach Dol?

183
15:27.720 --> 15:29.140
Shit. We're in trouble.

184
15:29.430 --> 15:30.490
Look at this.

185
15:52.700 --> 15:53.670
Guys...

186
16:08.980 --> 16:14.560
[K-2101 Bangkok]

187
16:14.600 --> 16:15.570
The call won't go through.

188
16:16.150 --> 16:18.170
Master must still be in the forest.

189
16:19.480 --> 16:20.530
Give him time.

190
16:20.880 --> 16:22.850
He promised he'd contact us.

191
16:28.540 --> 16:29.260
Khem.

192
16:46.120 --> 16:47.760
What are you seeing now?

193
16:51.660 --> 16:52.860
Is something wrong?

194
17:16.060 --> 17:18.180
You cleared that graveyard out thoroughly.

195
17:18.960 --> 17:21.190
Naturally. That's my expertise.

196
17:24.230 --> 17:24.849
Wait.

197
17:25.420 --> 17:26.240
A graveyard?

198
17:27.970 --> 17:29.360
This place is a graveyard?

199
17:30.390 --> 17:31.800
Nobody mentioned that.

200
17:34.810 --> 17:35.760
It used to be.

201
17:38.340 --> 17:40.070
Most of the spirits here are unclaimed,

202
17:40.630 --> 17:41.990
but they mean no harm.

203
17:42.670 --> 17:44.180
Perhaps they were given proper funeral rites

204
17:44.210 --> 17:46.950
by an undertaker with spiritual knowledge.

205
17:50.090 --> 17:51.630
If you were minding your own business,

206
17:52.260 --> 17:54.030
and someone evicted you from your home,

207
17:54.920 --> 17:56.070
how would you feel?

208
17:58.800 --> 18:01.100
Those spirits have gathered elsewhere now.

209
18:01.500 --> 18:03.540
The reason Charn can't trace Coach Dol's presence

210
18:05.550 --> 18:07.410
is that multiple spirits

211
18:08.720 --> 18:10.440
are cloaking his life force.

212
18:12.550 --> 18:13.690
Focus your minds

213
18:14.790 --> 18:17.200
toward where those spirits have gathered,

214
18:18.090 --> 18:19.190
and you'll find him.

215
18:26.140 --> 18:27.740
How are things on your end?

216
18:28.300 --> 18:30.560
You're here in spirit form,

217
18:30.990 --> 18:33.060
so that means you're still in the border forest, right?

218
18:34.440 --> 18:35.170
Yeah.

219
18:36.050 --> 18:36.830
I am.

220
18:40.480 --> 18:43.280
I've managed to help some of them.

221
18:44.220 --> 18:45.360
Don't worry.

222
18:45.650 --> 18:46.920
How can I not worry?

223
18:51.540 --> 18:52.760
I already know

224
18:53.240 --> 18:54.470
about Monk Kasem's warning.

225
18:57.340 --> 18:58.220
Since when

226
18:59.180 --> 19:00.810
did you start keeping secrets from me?

227
19:07.730 --> 19:09.490
I shouldn't have let you take this job.

228
19:15.510 --> 19:16.500
I'm sorry.

229
19:19.000 --> 19:21.380
But I'm glad I listened to you.

230
19:24.090 --> 19:25.510
If I hadn't stepped in,

231
19:26.860 --> 19:29.280
even more lives would have been lost.

232
19:44.400 --> 19:45.630
Once I'm done here,

233
19:46.650 --> 19:48.500
I'll come back to you as soon as I can.

234
19:57.530 --> 19:58.720
I promised you

235
20:00.230 --> 20:01.790
I'd make it back alive.

236
20:04.490 --> 20:06.370
I always keep my promises.

237
20:06.920 --> 20:07.870
You know that.

238
20:47.880 --> 20:49.900
Why don't you get out of here first?

239
20:50.040 --> 20:50.760
Come on.

240
20:52.530 --> 20:53.800
We can't.

241
20:54.230 --> 20:55.440
Oh, okay.

242
20:55.910 --> 20:57.580
Then... drink some water.

243
20:57.610 --> 20:58.760
It'll help you feel refreshed.

244
20:59.000 --> 21:00.790
Then we can figure out what to do next.

245
21:01.620 --> 21:03.230
I want to help them...

246
21:04.030 --> 21:05.720
We need to save Max.

247
21:06.790 --> 21:09.260
We don't even know where he is now.

248
21:09.400 --> 21:10.320
We kept going in circles.

249
21:14.650 --> 21:15.590
Master,

250
21:15.920 --> 21:17.800
the kids refuse to leave.

251
21:17.880 --> 21:20.520
They want us to find their friends first,

252
21:20.840 --> 21:22.300
or they won't leave.

253
21:29.520 --> 21:30.510
Give me your wrist.

254
21:34.700 --> 21:35.430
Come on.

255
21:48.210 --> 21:49.060
Give me your wrist.

256
21:58.020 --> 21:58.850
I know

257
21:59.800 --> 22:01.510
you're scared out of your minds.

258
22:02.290 --> 22:04.060
If you want your friends to survive,

259
22:04.260 --> 22:05.600
pull yourselves together.

260
22:07.130 --> 22:09.910
Your testimony is what will save them.

261
22:16.160 --> 22:16.840
Come on.

262
22:17.350 --> 22:18.310
Up on your feet.

263
22:27.030 --> 22:27.740
So,

264
22:28.850 --> 22:30.820
can you tell us

265
22:31.070 --> 22:34.620
how you got lost so deep in this forest?

266
22:43.200 --> 22:45.620
When Pond came to drive us home,

267
22:46.420 --> 22:48.660
we asked him to pull over so we could pee.

268
22:49.740 --> 22:51.710
Max came along with us.

269
22:52.100 --> 22:53.200
Then, out of nowhere,

270
22:53.230 --> 22:55.040
he heard something strange and went to check.

271
22:56.720 --> 22:57.700
When we realized

272
22:58.470 --> 23:00.210
he'd been gone for too long,

273
23:01.170 --> 23:03.700
we all went in after him.

274
23:06.330 --> 23:07.150
Quit whining.

275
23:09.140 --> 23:09.970
Move it.

276
23:11.710 --> 23:12.540
Walk.

277
23:12.630 --> 23:13.460
Keep moving.

278
23:13.860 --> 23:14.940
- Hey. - Get up.

279
23:14.960 --> 23:16.540
- Get up and move. - Move.

280
23:16.560 --> 23:17.080
Get up.

281
23:20.250 --> 23:21.260
Max, what are you filming?

282
23:21.290 --> 23:21.950
Shit.

283
23:22.120 --> 23:23.070
What?

284
23:23.120 --> 23:23.830
Max...

285
23:25.140 --> 23:26.320
- Hey. - Get up.

286
23:26.360 --> 23:27.400
- Get up and move. - Move.

287
23:27.420 --> 23:29.240
- Max... - Max.

288
23:29.270 --> 23:31.450
Shit, is this human trafficking?

289
23:31.950 --> 23:32.320
Shit.

290
23:32.340 --> 23:34.480
- Hey, what's your problem? - This is human trafficking,

291
23:34.510 --> 23:36.570
not some petty gambling. Knock it off, man.

292
23:36.600 --> 23:38.340
Yeah, drop it before we all get screwed.

293
23:38.370 --> 23:40.430
Guys, if we do nothing,

294
23:40.480 --> 23:42.080
we're no better than them.

295
23:42.100 --> 23:43.570
- It's not your job to do this. - This is no time to play the hero.

296
23:43.600 --> 23:45.340
- I'm taking this footage to the police. - Max, come on...

297
23:45.790 --> 23:47.810
Guys, you done yet? Back in the car.

298
23:49.200 --> 23:49.830
Hey.

299
23:52.140 --> 23:52.860
Who's that?

300
23:53.510 --> 23:54.330
Shit.

301
23:57.070 --> 23:57.880
Shit.

302
23:57.910 --> 23:59.020
Run!

303
23:59.660 --> 24:00.460
Stop.

304
24:00.490 --> 24:01.550
Don't follow them.

305
24:17.740 --> 24:29.250
[Incanting]

306
25:02.510 --> 25:03.380
Baitong...

307
25:14.880 --> 25:15.690
Pond,

308
25:17.000 --> 25:18.370
missing your wife?

309
25:26.590 --> 25:27.320
Yeah.

310
25:36.560 --> 25:37.920
She's pregnant, too.

311
25:51.270 --> 25:53.430
If I don't make it out of here tonight,

312
25:57.320 --> 25:59.710
could you give Baitong this ring?

313
26:03.530 --> 26:04.850
Come on, man.

314
26:06.900 --> 26:09.730
Give it to her yourself.

315
26:11.330 --> 26:12.850
We're making it out of here together.

316
26:23.610 --> 26:25.280
Come here. Bring it in.

317
26:27.090 --> 26:28.050
Pond, come on.

318
26:31.310 --> 26:32.930
- Pond. - Come on.

319
26:37.780 --> 26:38.720
Come on, man.

320
26:43.600 --> 26:45.770
- Watch the wound. - Sorry.

321
26:47.000 --> 26:48.000
By tomorrow morning,

322
26:49.230 --> 26:50.590
we'll make it out together.

323
26:59.290 --> 27:00.730
Coach Dol is somewhere here,

324
27:00.910 --> 27:02.440
but his soul is fading.

325
27:03.650 --> 27:04.630
Follow me.

326
27:18.280 --> 27:20.300
It's pretty creepy here.

327
27:21.910 --> 27:24.180
This feels like a test of courage

328
27:24.430 --> 27:26.120
in those childhood cartoons.

329
27:36.180 --> 27:37.780
Yeah, just think of it

330
27:38.130 --> 27:40.460
as one of those cartoons we used to watch.

331
27:40.710 --> 27:41.430
Right?

332
27:41.550 --> 27:43.330
What cartoon has ghosts right in your face like this?

333
27:43.350 --> 27:44.020
Jet!

334
27:44.610 --> 27:47.040
Must be nice being grounded and seeing nothing.

335
27:48.770 --> 27:49.680
Stop talking.

336
27:57.010 --> 27:57.870
Coach Dol...

337
27:58.760 --> 27:59.760
- Coach Dol? - Oh...

338
28:03.450 --> 28:04.680
[It's always me]

339
28:04.700 --> 28:05.730
Coach Dol!

340
28:22.940 --> 28:24.290
How many of them are here?

341
28:24.450 --> 28:25.750
I can hardly breathe.

342
28:26.280 --> 28:27.150
Whoa...

343
28:29.620 --> 28:30.520
At least a dozen.

344
28:32.260 --> 28:33.300
Don't worry.

345
28:33.680 --> 28:34.590
I'll handle them.

346
28:36.630 --> 28:37.640
Wait, Jet.

347
28:38.100 --> 28:40.170
- What? - Remember what Master told us?

348
28:46.180 --> 28:47.910
Took you long enough.

349
28:54.870 --> 28:56.150
Who are you, Elder?

350
28:58.130 --> 28:59.710
I was this temple's undertaker.

351
29:00.530 --> 29:01.660
I've cremated hundreds

352
29:01.690 --> 29:03.180
and buried thousands.

353
29:03.740 --> 29:06.690
Made merit for every unclaimed body.

354
29:07.510 --> 29:08.640
I entered their dreams

355
29:08.670 --> 29:10.440
and haunted their set,

356
29:10.630 --> 29:11.980
yet they still wouldn't leave.

357
29:12.270 --> 29:13.570
We were minding our own business,

358
29:13.660 --> 29:15.840
and you came stomping all over the place,

359
29:15.860 --> 29:17.120
making a racket.

360
29:19.900 --> 29:21.900
We're here to apologize on the crew's behalf.

361
29:22.510 --> 29:25.180
Nobody meant any disrespect.

362
29:26.880 --> 29:28.630
Please let our director go.

363
29:28.660 --> 29:30.300
Your director's the worst one.

364
29:30.320 --> 29:32.060
Everyone else was ready to pack up,

365
29:32.080 --> 29:34.240
but he kept refusing to leave,

366
29:34.260 --> 29:35.460
whining about missing the air date.

367
29:36.790 --> 29:38.040
Come on, Elder.

368
29:38.790 --> 29:41.280
We already asked for permission.

369
29:41.520 --> 29:43.630
Cut us some slack, please.

370
29:43.660 --> 29:44.460
Jet!

371
29:45.000 --> 29:47.540
Just because you asked doesn't mean you get it.

372
29:52.200 --> 29:53.560
What are they trying to do?

373
29:58.200 --> 29:59.710
To all the unclaimed spirits here,

374
30:00.930 --> 30:01.950
please...

375
30:02.260 --> 30:03.520
let me help you.

376
30:03.870 --> 30:05.320
Please.

377
30:20.390 --> 30:21.400
Malatang?

378
30:21.430 --> 30:22.220
Sure thing.

379
30:22.240 --> 30:24.340
I'll have the crew offer alms for you.

380
30:24.830 --> 30:26.650
Yeah, thank you.

381
30:32.340 --> 30:33.140
Hotpot?

382
30:33.170 --> 30:33.960
You got it.

383
30:33.990 --> 30:36.130
I'll have the crew offer that with the alms.

384
30:51.380 --> 30:52.590
He's only asleep,

385
30:52.840 --> 30:54.280
but lingering among us for too long

386
30:54.300 --> 30:56.200
isn't good for the living.

387
30:56.780 --> 30:58.720
How you revive him is your concern.

388
30:59.510 --> 31:00.340
So...

389
31:01.140 --> 31:03.300
is there anything we can do for you?

390
31:03.330 --> 31:04.150
No.

391
31:04.510 --> 31:06.150
All I want is peace.

392
31:06.490 --> 31:07.630
Come daybreak,

393
31:08.250 --> 31:09.620
pack up and leave.

394
31:12.640 --> 31:13.690
Thank you.

395
31:27.120 --> 31:28.510
Slow down, Khao.

396
31:29.200 --> 31:30.080
You holding up?

397
31:31.570 --> 31:32.370
Wait...

398
31:33.150 --> 31:35.590
Isn't that where we came in?

399
31:35.880 --> 31:36.880
Did we make it?

400
31:36.910 --> 31:37.710
Hold on.

401
31:38.800 --> 31:40.480
Something feels off.

402
31:41.140 --> 31:42.480
It's way too quiet.

403
31:42.670 --> 31:44.260
Not even a bird is chirping.

404
31:45.340 --> 31:47.400
Should we go back to where we were?

405
31:49.570 --> 31:50.240
No.

406
31:50.930 --> 31:51.960
I say we keep going.

407
31:52.370 --> 31:53.460
Max's wound is too bad.

408
31:54.820 --> 32:01.080
[Incanting]

409
32:01.100 --> 32:01.580
Max.

410
32:01.610 --> 32:02.810
- Hey. - Max!

411
32:02.840 --> 32:04.380
- Max... - Max.

412
32:04.410 --> 32:07.470
Khao, what do we do?

413
32:07.500 --> 32:08.740
Khao!

414
32:08.990 --> 32:09.830
Shit.

415
32:09.860 --> 32:15.170
[Incanting]

416
32:15.200 --> 32:15.930
Max.

417
32:15.960 --> 32:19.060
[Incanting]

418
32:21.380 --> 32:22.170
Khao!

419
32:22.360 --> 32:23.290
Khao...

420
32:28.670 --> 32:40.450
[Incanting]

421
32:51.400 --> 33:11.880
[Incanting]

422
33:17.990 --> 33:18.910
Stop.

423
33:24.350 --> 33:24.990
Max...

424
33:26.560 --> 33:28.190
Unless you want to suffer the same fate,

425
33:29.010 --> 33:30.410
go back to where you belong,

426
33:31.390 --> 33:33.270
and I shall release your soul.

427
33:51.400 --> 33:52.170
Guys!

428
33:52.190 --> 33:53.180
Hang in there.

429
33:53.210 --> 33:54.430
Hey!

430
33:56.790 --> 33:57.550
- How are you? - Hey.

431
33:57.580 --> 33:58.090
You okay?

432
33:58.120 --> 33:59.790
- Max can't take it. - Hang in there, Max.

433
33:59.900 --> 34:00.790
Max.

434
34:01.730 --> 34:03.040
I'm right here.

435
34:03.070 --> 34:04.040
Hang in there.

436
34:04.070 --> 34:05.650
Stay with us. We're right here.

437
34:05.670 --> 34:06.570
Calm down.

438
34:07.150 --> 34:08.960
Stay with me! Look at me, keep looking at me!

439
34:54.010 --> 34:54.920
We're safe.

440
34:57.290 --> 34:58.150
We made it.

441
34:58.610 --> 34:59.780
We're going home.

442
35:00.100 --> 35:00.900
We're safe.

443
35:02.440 --> 35:03.660
- Easy. - Up you go.

444
35:03.990 --> 35:04.720
Okay.

445
35:07.520 --> 35:09.090
- Great. - Okay.

446
35:10.290 --> 35:11.500
- Hang on. - Take a deep breath.

447
35:11.530 --> 35:13.010
Lean on me.

448
35:13.430 --> 35:14.710
Easy, alright.

449
35:18.300 --> 35:19.490
Thank you, Master.

450
35:20.340 --> 35:22.070
Make sure to bathe in holy water when you get home.

451
35:22.640 --> 35:24.300
We're going home, guys.

452
35:26.220 --> 35:27.280
We're finally going home.

453
35:34.950 --> 35:35.820
Master!

454
35:51.890 --> 35:54.310
Make sure you have the doctor examine you again.

455
35:55.950 --> 35:57.760
- Okay. - Take good care of yourself.

456
35:59.190 --> 36:00.640
Goodbye.

457
36:05.410 --> 36:07.630
Do I really have to do all this for those ghosts?

458
36:08.710 --> 36:09.760
I'm counting on you.

459
36:11.710 --> 36:13.860
Alright, thanks so much either way.

460
36:14.340 --> 36:14.940
- See you. - Take care.

461
36:14.970 --> 36:15.510
Bye.

462
36:37.060 --> 36:38.480
What's wrong, Khem?

463
36:44.850 --> 36:45.690
It's just...

464
36:47.310 --> 36:48.550
My heart is racing.

465
36:50.030 --> 36:52.820
I have this weird feeling I can't explain.

466
36:54.880 --> 36:56.370
You barely got any sleep

467
36:57.140 --> 36:58.740
and drank all that coffee.

468
36:59.690 --> 37:01.010
Of course your heart is racing.

469
37:04.310 --> 37:05.270
That's not the reason.

470
37:06.930 --> 37:07.910
What's with you guys?

471
37:11.100 --> 37:12.030
Master...

472
37:12.840 --> 37:14.100
I sense that he's...

473
37:29.350 --> 37:30.200
Master!

474
37:41.320 --> 37:43.410
Pierced right through enchanted skin.

475
37:43.840 --> 37:45.490
This sorcerer's bullets

476
37:45.520 --> 37:46.570
actually work.

477
37:49.370 --> 37:50.650
Thanks, Master,

478
37:50.760 --> 37:52.910
for tracking down these kids for us.

479
37:56.820 --> 38:02.060
[Incanting]

480
38:02.090 --> 38:03.240
- It burns... - It's burning hot...

481
38:03.270 --> 38:09.800
[Incanting]

482
38:12.010 --> 38:14.360
Still got fight in you, huh?

483
38:14.600 --> 38:15.760
In that case,

484
38:17.820 --> 38:19.820
I'll finish you off first.

485
38:35.920 --> 38:37.110
First blood!

486
38:38.350 --> 38:39.300
Stop right there!

487
38:40.100 --> 38:40.760
Hey, stop.

488
38:40.780 --> 38:41.560
Stop!

489
38:41.590 --> 38:42.540
- Hey! - Freeze.

490
38:47.470 --> 38:49.050
Surprise, baby.

491
38:50.700 --> 38:51.840
Get up.

492
38:54.690 --> 38:56.490
I missed you, bro.

493
38:56.510 --> 38:57.840
Ow, that hurts.

494
38:58.710 --> 39:00.400
Takes me back to our vocational school days.

495
39:00.880 --> 39:02.080
Without me,

496
39:02.100 --> 39:03.650
you wouldn't have made it once again.

497
39:03.840 --> 39:05.760
You're late, and you're still trying to look cool?

498
39:05.930 --> 39:06.770
Come on.

499
39:07.360 --> 39:08.800
If not for me,

500
39:09.280 --> 39:11.260
who else could've tracked you down, bro?

501
39:11.680 --> 39:13.360
Those marks you made on the trees

502
39:13.390 --> 39:15.490
were as faint as cat scratches.

503
39:21.670 --> 39:22.440
You...

504
39:22.670 --> 39:23.480
Go to hell.

505
39:23.780 --> 39:24.230
Shit.

506
39:24.260 --> 39:27.280
Stop!

507
39:48.790 --> 39:51.420
Hey, you're still worried, Khem?

508
39:53.950 --> 39:55.200
I believe

509
39:55.560 --> 39:58.400
the ancestral spirits will watch over Master.

510
40:07.650 --> 40:09.770
You trust him anyway.

511
40:11.060 --> 40:12.120
No matter what,

512
40:12.440 --> 40:13.670
he'll be safe

513
40:13.700 --> 40:15.640
and come back to marry you.

514
40:38.780 --> 40:39.560
Peem?

515
40:40.710 --> 40:41.740
Peem...

516
40:48.220 --> 40:49.150
Peem.

517
40:52.070 --> 40:52.890
Peem!

518
40:57.650 --> 40:58.390
Is this...

519
40:58.950 --> 41:00.110
really you?

520
41:00.310 --> 41:01.240
You're not a ghost, are you?

521
41:01.260 --> 41:02.790
Is this your spirit form?

522
41:02.810 --> 41:05.570
Why are you covered in so many wounds?

523
41:05.600 --> 41:08.000
Are you alright? What about...

524
41:10.960 --> 41:12.130
I'm back.

525
41:31.220 --> 41:32.800
Hi, I'm back.

526
41:33.620 --> 41:35.070
Coming all the way here, huh?

527
41:35.370 --> 41:37.570
Yeah, just a phone call would do.

528
41:37.810 --> 41:38.650
Sorry.

529
41:38.820 --> 41:39.690
My phone died.

530
41:39.950 --> 41:42.250
Someone insisted on catching the first flight out,

531
41:42.280 --> 41:43.930
refusing to even see a doctor.

532
41:44.470 --> 41:46.000
Down so bad, it's ridiculous.

533
41:47.510 --> 41:49.090
More wounds?

534
41:51.300 --> 41:53.190
At least let me know what you're doing.

535
41:56.260 --> 41:58.400
How did you even end up with these?

536
42:01.300 --> 42:01.790
Go to hell.

537
42:01.820 --> 42:03.300
Stop!

538
42:18.680 --> 42:19.880
I told you to stop.

539
42:20.330 --> 42:22.650
Paran has protective tattoos that make him impervious to blades.

540
42:29.980 --> 42:30.810
Stop.

541
42:35.060 --> 42:35.910
That's enough.

542
42:39.770 --> 42:41.500
Don't burden your soul with more sins.

543
43:26.250 --> 43:27.400
Thank you.

544
43:29.070 --> 43:31.380
May you journey to a peaceful realm.

545
43:36.890 --> 43:38.600
Let your karma guide your way.

546
43:56.590 --> 43:57.450
Hello.

547
43:58.940 --> 43:59.840
You got lucky.

548
44:02.280 --> 44:03.230
We made it.

549
44:04.330 --> 44:05.130
We're safe.

550
44:05.300 --> 44:06.590
Watch his wound.

551
44:07.160 --> 44:08.250
- I... - We're going home.

552
44:08.280 --> 44:10.040
I won't go on another trip with you guys again.

553
44:10.730 --> 44:12.340
- Let's go! - Stay awake!

554
44:18.130 --> 44:19.230
What are you laughing at?

555
44:19.260 --> 44:20.770
Cut it out.

556
44:20.790 --> 44:22.040
If you don't, I'll laugh, too.

557
44:28.770 --> 44:29.600
Move!

558
44:29.780 --> 44:30.520
Keep walking!

559
44:30.550 --> 44:31.250
Move!

560
44:31.430 --> 44:32.290
It's over now.

561
44:35.540 --> 44:36.790
Time to go home.

562
44:38.060 --> 44:39.260
Your parents must be worried sick.

563
44:43.860 --> 44:44.850
Look at Pond.

564
44:46.490 --> 44:47.900
He must be exhausted.

565
44:48.610 --> 44:49.580
Wake up.

566
44:49.600 --> 44:50.110
Pond.

567
44:50.140 --> 44:51.250
It's all over.

568
44:51.420 --> 44:52.780
- Pond. - Pond.

569
44:53.560 --> 44:54.360
Hey, Pond.

570
44:59.460 --> 45:00.200
Shit.

571
45:01.520 --> 45:02.430
What's wrong with him?

572
45:02.830 --> 45:03.840
He's been shot.

573
45:04.810 --> 45:05.290
Pond...

574
45:05.320 --> 45:06.320
- What happened? - Pond.

575
45:06.350 --> 45:07.470
- Pond. - Hey.

576
45:07.830 --> 45:08.540
Pond!

577
45:08.560 --> 45:09.930
- Pond, what happened to you? - Wake up.

578
45:09.950 --> 45:11.470
- Come on, wake up. - Pond...

579
45:11.500 --> 45:12.570
- Pond, hey. - Talk to me.

580
45:12.600 --> 45:14.320
- What happened to him? - Pond, wake up.

581
45:15.870 --> 45:18.510
- Master, what happened to him? - Pond.

582
45:18.530 --> 45:19.980
- Hey, press on the wound. - Why is he like this?

583
45:20.010 --> 45:22.230
- Master... - Pond, please wake up.

584
45:22.260 --> 45:24.300
You have to come home with me.

585
45:25.120 --> 45:26.750
- Pond. - Please help him.

586
45:34.860 --> 45:36.790
Now they can go home to their parents.

587
45:39.240 --> 45:42.210
You died because of me.

588
45:46.140 --> 45:47.130
It's not your fault.

589
45:50.690 --> 45:52.090
It's my fault for making noise,

590
45:53.940 --> 45:55.670
and that got the kids hunted down.

591
45:56.680 --> 45:58.890
Master, please help him.

592
46:01.710 --> 46:03.650
You also ended up hurt.

593
46:24.360 --> 46:26.220
Baitong's health is delicate.

594
46:30.630 --> 46:34.860
Please pray for her so she can deliver our baby safely.

595
46:50.770 --> 46:53.270
Master, can you please help him?

596
46:55.340 --> 46:56.950
Pond, please wake up.

597
46:56.980 --> 46:59.270
You have to come home with me.

598
47:07.990 --> 47:10.150
Pond, please wake up.

599
47:22.240 --> 47:24.400
Thank you for giving your life to save Peem.

600
47:25.990 --> 47:27.730
Even though we never met,

601
47:29.400 --> 47:31.330
I will always dedicate merit to you.

602
47:39.580 --> 47:41.720
May the merit you have earned

603
47:41.980 --> 47:44.340
guide you to a better realm,

604
47:45.070 --> 47:46.420
where you find stillness,

605
47:46.710 --> 47:48.100
serenity, and peace,

606
47:49.560 --> 47:51.580
and may you leave this world free of all worries.

607
48:03.110 --> 48:04.360
- That's enough. - What?

608
48:04.390 --> 48:05.050
It hurts.

609
48:05.070 --> 48:06.860
Come on, bear with it, Master.

610
48:06.880 --> 48:08.190
This might be our last chance to see each other.

611
48:12.170 --> 48:12.950
Yes?

612
48:13.190 --> 48:14.360
Are you jinxing me?

613
48:16.270 --> 48:17.190
Not at all.

614
48:22.660 --> 48:23.640
Hey, Charn.

615
48:24.190 --> 48:25.110
It's gorgeous over there.

616
48:25.140 --> 48:26.060
- Wanna take some photos? - But...

617
48:26.090 --> 48:28.570
Over there. We can even feed the fish.

618
48:28.600 --> 48:29.520
Take a look.

619
48:29.950 --> 48:31.130
It's perfect, isn't it?

620
49:37.630 --> 49:39.290
Until the wedding,

621
49:41.330 --> 49:43.400
should I just stop you from taking any more jobs?

622
49:45.980 --> 49:48.180
Whenever you do, I can't reach you.

623
49:50.530 --> 49:52.330
If anything happens to you,

624
49:53.190 --> 49:54.510
how am I supposed to go on?

625
50:05.550 --> 50:06.700
I'm sorry.

626
50:14.360 --> 50:15.620
Whether it's now

627
50:17.110 --> 50:18.910
or after we're married,

628
50:20.620 --> 50:22.850
I'll tell you everything.

629
50:28.680 --> 50:30.300
If I ever have to save someone,

630
50:32.620 --> 50:34.000
I won't put my life on the line.

631
50:36.910 --> 50:38.680
I won't make you worry again.

632
50:53.230 --> 50:54.300
In this life,

633
50:56.940 --> 50:59.360
I will never let you be torn from the one you love again.

634
51:09.400 --> 51:10.460
And in this life,

635
51:12.580 --> 51:14.160
you won't be lonely,

636
51:16.810 --> 51:19.180
nor will you have to bear the pain alone, either.

637
51:33.300 --> 51:35.390
No more risking your life like that.

638
52:41.720 --> 52:43.980
Keep moving, everybody.

639
52:53.590 --> 52:55.820
Keep going, everybody.

640
52:55.840 --> 52:57.130
Show them what you've got!

641
53:00.360 --> 53:01.000
Hey.

642
53:01.720 --> 53:02.470
Jet.

643
53:02.500 --> 53:04.400
Hold it steady, or you'll drop the betrothal tray.

644
53:04.420 --> 53:06.860
Can't help it. These hips move faster than 5G internet.

645
53:06.880 --> 53:09.340
Once the beat drops, they automatically sync up!

646
53:10.380 --> 53:11.320
I know

647
53:11.880 --> 53:15.000
my disciple can tell what's proper and what's not.

648
53:17.320 --> 53:19.170
Yes, desynced now.

649
54:11.050 --> 54:12.190
All done.

650
54:13.080 --> 54:14.600
You look gorgeous, Khem.

651
54:15.110 --> 54:16.120
Khem,

652
54:17.410 --> 54:18.580
someone's here to see you.

653
54:44.230 --> 54:45.080
Father...

654
54:47.750 --> 54:48.830
How do I look?

655
54:49.990 --> 54:51.600
You look wonderful, my son.

656
55:04.650 --> 55:05.680
Khem.

657
55:06.790 --> 55:08.570
Your groom is here.

658
56:10.320 --> 56:13.740
At long last, we're finally one family.

659
56:14.760 --> 56:16.560
I love you more than anything, Khem.

660
56:17.000 --> 56:19.230
I love you, too. More than anything in the world.

661
56:22.680 --> 56:23.470
Mom,

662
56:23.540 --> 56:25.750
would it be okay if I stayed in Bangkok with Charn

663
56:25.770 --> 56:27.200
for about a month?

664
56:27.710 --> 56:29.450
Every time I wake up, he's already gone.

665
56:29.550 --> 56:31.400
You should clear things up with him.

666
56:31.740 --> 56:34.150
Once this task's done, you'll have another one lined up.

667
56:34.290 --> 56:35.840
When will you ever have time for me?

668
